/// ErrorReason — the raw reason of a transport `Result error:`.
///
/// A transport's error is an Exception when it comes from an Erlang
/// `{error, R}` (its `reason` is `R`, BT-3954), but a plain value when the
/// transport built the `Result error:` itself (`#not_secure`, or a fake
/// transport in a test). Code that classifies errors, like the acceptor,
/// asks this class instead of assuming either.
///
/// ## Examples
/// ```beamtalk
/// ErrorReason of: #emfile                                         // => #emfile
/// ErrorReason of: ((Erlang file) read_file: "/no/such/file") error // => #enoent
/// ```
sealed Object subclass: ErrorReason

  /// `anError reason` for an Exception, otherwise `anError` itself.
  class sealed of: anError :: Object -> Object =>
    (anError isKindOf: Exception) ifTrue: [anError reason] ifFalse: [anError]
